        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260504-mali-crisis-junta-entrenches-itself-with-no-political-solution-in-sight",
        "orario": "17:24",
        "timestamp": 1777908279,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Mali crisis: Junta entrenches itself with no political solution in sight Issued on: 04/05/2026 - 17:24 Modified: 04/05/2026 - 17:36 It has been more than a week since jihadist and separatist forces in Mali launched a major military campaign aimed at ousting the ruling junta. On the first day of the offensive, Mali’s defence minister was killed. Since then, rebels have seized a strategic military stronghold in the north and are now attempting to blockade the capital, Bamako. FRANCE 24 terrorism expert Wassim Nasr explains the latest developments. Allies jolted on defence as Trump pulls troops from Germany 04/05/2026 Philippines: Massive ash cloud fills sky as volcano erupts 04/05/2026 NATO chief says Europeans have 'gotten message' from Trump on defence 04/05/2026 Shares of eBay take off on a $56 billion buyout bid from GameStop's Ryan Cohen 04/05/2026 The loyal, lonely keepers of Sudan's pyramids 04/05/2026 Former New York Mayor Giuliani hospitalised in critical condition 04/05/2026 ‘Far beyond’ EU and NATO: Armenia hosts EPC summit cast as ‘gateway’ in shifting diplomatic order 04/05/2026 Europe US to 'guide' stranded ships from Hormuz: What we know about 'Project Freedom' 04/05/2026 Hantavirus: Three cruise ship passengers die in suspected outbreak 04/05/2026"
