        "timestamp": 1777909364,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement United States World United States & Canada Trump family’s crypto project sues billionaire backer Justin Sun The Trumps’ World Liberty Financial accused Sun of launching a ‘public smear campaign’ 1 -MIN READ 1 -MIN Listen Reuters Published: 11:42pm, 4 May 2026 World Liberty ⁠Financial, the crypto venture co-founded ⁠by US President Donald Trump and his sons, said on Monday it had filed a defamation lawsuit against Hong Kong-based crypto entrepreneur Justin Sun, in the latest escalation of a dispute ‌between the project and one of its most prominent backers. World Liberty posted a copy of its lawsuit on X in which it accused Sun of launching a “public smear campaign” including claims that it said were false. The crypto project – one of several lucrative crypto businesses ⁠co-founded or controlled by the Trump family – said that Sun had done things ‌he was not allowed to do with his tokens, including transferring them to crypto exchange Binance. What is Polymarket, the gambling site that lets you bet on almost everything? What is Polymarket, the gambling site that lets you bet on almost everything? In April, Sun sued World ‌Liberty Financial saying the company had illegally frozen the tokens he ⁠had bought. ⁠Sun said World Liberty secretly installed tools to prevent the sale of his tokens after they ‌became tradeable in September 2025. Advertisement In its lawsuit, World Liberty said its ability to freeze tokens had ‌been disclosed ‌in the Terms of Sale. Sun said: “The alleged defamation lawsuit ‌that World Liberty announced on X today is nothing more than a ⁠meritless PR stunt. I stand by my actions and look forward to defeating ⁠the case in court.” He posted the same message on X. Advertisement The president’s son, Donald Trump Jnr, reposted World Liberty’s thread, with the ‌comment “Read this entire ‌thread for the truth!!!!” Zach Witkoff, World Liberty’s chief executive and a co-founder, said on X, “I look forward to the truth coming out in court.” Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
